    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "Full build is green. \n\nI implemented the \"no-future-date\" rule for `POST /api/owners` following the project's OfficeFloor conventions:\n\n1. **`FutureRegistrationDateException`** (checked, `extends Exception`) \u2014 thrown when a supplied `registrationDate` is later than the server date.\n\n2. **`FutureRegistrationDateExceptionHandler`** \u2014 responds `400 Bad Request` with `{\"errors\":[\"registrationDate\"]}`, matching the existing validation handlers.\n\n3. **Escalation YAML** \u2014 `officefloor/escalation/\u2026FutureRegistrationDateException.yml` wiring the exception to its handler (the `@ControllerAdvice` equivalent).\n\n4. **`BuildOwner`** \u2014 where the effective registration date is already computed, it now throws the exception when a *supplied* date is after `LocalDate.now()`, before rolling it onto a business day. A `null` (omitted) date still defaults to the server date, so only future dates are rejected.\n\n`Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` and `BUILD SUCCESS`.",
